# Engine contract

The platform mandates a **contract**, not a specific inference product. Any
serving runtime that meets this contract may be used. Concrete engines
(e.g. Triton) are named only in consumer foundations and ADRs.

## Contract requirements

An inference engine on device must:

1. Expose a **Prometheus and/or OpenTelemetry metrics endpoint** the agent can
   scrape (passive sidecar / pull — preferred so model-team code stays
   untouched).
2. Support **model-repository-style hot load/unload** so shadow and switch
   need no container restart when headroom allows.
3. Publish a scrapeable **active model version** fact (and shadow role when
   applicable) so the agent's reported device/slot state stays truthful after
   the model team switches.

### Recommended active-version metric shape

Serving clients generated from `edge-triton-client-foundation` (and any
engine that wants agent interop) SHOULD expose:

| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| Name | `edge_model_role_info` |
| Type | Gauge |
| Value | `1` when loaded in that role; `0` when cleared |
| Labels | `model`, `version`, `role` where `role` ∈ `{active, shadow}` |

The agent infers `shadow-running` / `promoted` / `reverted` from this scrape
plus liveness — it does not call engine-internal switch APIs.

## Ownership seam

| Owner | Responsibility |
|-------|----------------|
| **Agent (platform)** | Deliver artifact, start/stop engine **containers**, scrape metrics, report milestones, govern resources |
| **Engine (model team)** | Load/shadow/switch/unload models, evaluate quality, expose metrics + active version |

If (3) is missing, the agent's state goes stale the instant the model team
switches — this readout is the contract between "model team switches" and
"agent reports state."

## Agent scrape behaviour

- Prefer **pull** (scrape) over requiring model-team push into the agent.
- Infer milestones (`shadow-running`, `promoted`, `reverted`) from scraped
  facts + liveness — do not call engine-internal switch APIs to "confirm"
  decisions the agent does not own.

